# The build context is an allow list: everything is left out, then only what `go build ./cmd/shift2eu`
# needs is let back in. Later lines win, so the exclusions at the end apply inside the allowed paths too.
*

!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd/
!internal/

# Tests and their fixtures are not built into the binary. The catalog snapshots the targets embed
# (internal/adapter/target/*/catalog.json) are not test data and stay in.
**/*_test.go
**/testdata

# Named explicitly as well, so they stay out if the allow list above is ever loosened: git data,
# worktrees, local builds, coverage reports, credentials.
.git
.worktrees
bin
dist
coverage.out
coverage.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.envrc
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*credentials*.json
**/*service-account*.json
**/.aws
**/.azure
**/.config/gcloud

# Real inventories and reports describe someone's infrastructure (CLAUDE.md rule 2): no layer may hold
# one. Matches file names only, so the internal/adapter/report packages are kept.
inventories
reports
**/*inventory*.json
**/*report*.json
**/*report*.md
**/*report*.html
